        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): prefer configured slash command",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes Slack slash commands timing out when an explicit tenant command is configured while native Slack commands are enabled.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe Slack monitor treated native commands and the configured tenant command as mutually exclusive, but checked native commands first:\n\n```ts\nif (nativeCommands.length > 0) {\n  // register native commands\n} else if (slashCommand.enabled) {\n  // register configured command\n}\n```\n\nBecause native commands are enabled by default, an explicit command such as `/claw` was never registered. Slack routed the command to the app, but no Bolt handler acknowledged it, so users saw the generic \"app did not respond\" failure.\n\n## Fix\n\nKeep the command modes mutually exclusive, but let explicit tenant configuration win:\n\n```ts\nif (slashCommand.enabled) {\n  // register configured command\n} else if (nativeCommands.length > 0) {\n  // register native commands\n}\n```\n\nThe regression test verifies that an enabled configured slash command registers its matcher and does not also register native `/usage`.\n\n## Why the Runtime-Config Change Was Removed\n\nAn earlier revision added startup source-config matching around `getRuntimeConfigSnapshot()`. That was unnecessary and made the fix harder to reason about:\n\n- The live failure occurred before the slash handler ran, so it did not demonstrate a SecretRef/runtime-snapshot failure.\n- The runtime snapshot is already the current resolved runtime config.\n- Capturing a startup source config as a frozen identity anchor added special-case state without fixing the actual registration bug.\n\nThe final patch restores the straightforward runtime lookup:\n\n```ts\nconst cfg = getRuntimeConfigSnapshot() ?? ctx.cfg;\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the registration fix, `/claw status` returned Slack's generic \"app did not respond\" failure while Socket Mode and the app credentials were healthy.\n- After the registration fix, `/claw status` returned an ephemeral operational status response.\n- After the registration fix, `/claw help` returned the ephemeral help menu.\n- The successful live proof was on commit `92924d0`; the later runtime-config experiment was removed, so final head `d8f8522` retains the already-proven registration behavior.\n",
